{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "diffusers-nano-id-av",
      "prompt": "Run Cosmos3 inverse dynamics with the diffusers path on this machine's single GPU: predict the ego-motion trajectory of the AV clip bundled by the action entry skill (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/videos/av_0.mp4, relative to this skill directory) with nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano (guardrails disabled for this smoke), i.e. the skill's av_inverse_0 case, using a checkout of the public framework repository (https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git, branch main) for the pose helpers. Point the notebook's output root at outputs/ so the predicted action array lands at outputs/av_inverse_0/av_inverse_0_action.json, and record the predicted action shape in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "outputs/av_inverse_0/av_inverse_0_action.json holds the 60x9 action trajectory Cosmos3-Nano predicted for av_0.mp4 through Cosmos3OmniPipeline, and result_summary.md records the shape, settings, runtime and peak CUDA memory.",
      "assertions": [
        "A dedicated Python environment was created for diffusers per the skill and the run used it, not the system python",
        "nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano was loaded in bfloat16 on the GPU and the inverse_dynamics CosmosActionCondition was built from the bundled av_0.mp4 clip (chunk_size 60, domain av, resolution tier 480)",
        "outputs/av_inverse_0/av_inverse_0_action.json exists and holds a 60x9 numeric array written by the pipeline run recorded in the transcript",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the action file traces to a real pipeline run in the transcript",
        "result_summary.md reports the predicted action shape, the settings, wall-clock time and GPU memory actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/av_inverse_0/av_inverse_0_action.json",
          "min_bytes": 2000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "env setup",
        "model load",
        "inference",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "framework-nano-id-av",
      "prompt": "Run Cosmos3 inverse dynamics through the native cosmos_framework inference entrypoint on this machine's single GPU. Use a fresh clone of the public framework repository, https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git (branch main), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill; build the skill's AV inverse-dynamics spec for the clip bundled by the action entry skill (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/videos/av_0.mp4, relative to this skill directory) and run it with Cosmos3-Nano (guardrails disabled, seed 0). Point the notebook's output root at outputs/ so the result lands at outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json; record the exact command and the predicted action shape in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "cosmos_framework.scripts.inference completes on one GPU with Cosmos3-Nano from a fresh clone of the public framework main and writes outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json whose outputs[0].content.action is a 60x9 trajectory; result_summary.md records the command and runtime.",
      "assertions": [
        "Inference ran through cosmos_framework.scripts.inference from the framework venv with checkpoint Cosmos3-Nano on one GPU, as the skill documents it",
        "The framework checkout used for setup and inference is a fresh clone of the public NVIDIA/cosmos-framework main (the transcript shows the clone), not the skill snapshot",
        "A JSONL spec with one inverse_dynamics record (domain av, action_chunk_size 60, fps 10, image_size 480, absolute vision_path to the bundled av_0.mp4) was built per the documented schema and passed with -i",
        "outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json exists with status success and outputs[0].content.action holding a 60x9 numeric array",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the result file traces to a real inference run in the transcript, and result_summary.md contains the exact command line and the measured runtime"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json",
          "min_bytes": 2000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "spec build",
        "inference run",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vllm-omni-nano-id-av",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano with vLLM-Omni (guardrails disabled) and run ONE inverse-dynamics request through its video API for the AV clip bundled by the action entry skill (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/videos/av_0.mp4, relative to this skill directory), i.e. the skill's av_inverse_0 record. Point the notebook's output root at outputs/ so the result lands at outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json (with the server's action.json, response.json and final.json beside it), then stop the server. Record the server command, time-to-ready, request latency and the predicted action shape in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "The vLLM-Omni server comes up, one multipart /v1/videos inverse-dynamics request for av_0.mp4 completes, and outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json holds the 60x9 predicted action; result_summary.md records server command, readiness time, latency and shape.",
      "assertions": [
        "The vLLM-Omni server was started with the documented image, model and flags and reported the model on /v1/models before the request was sent",
        "The request was the documented multipart POST /v1/videos with action_mode inverse_dynamics, domain av, raw_action_dim 9 and the bundled av_0.mp4 as input_reference, polled on /v1/videos/{id} until completed",
        "outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json exists and holds a 60x9 numeric action array taken from the server's final response",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the action array traces to a real server response in the transcript, and the server was stopped at the end",
        "result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready, request latency and the predicted action shape"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json",
          "min_bytes": 2000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "inference request",
        "teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sglang-nano-id-av",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano with SGLang (guardrails disabled) and run ONE inverse-dynamics request through its action generation API for the AV clip bundled by the action entry skill (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/videos/av_0.mp4, relative to this skill directory), i.e. the skill's av_inverse_0 record. Wait until the server reports the model before sending the request. Point the notebook's output root at outputs/ so the result lands at outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json (with action.json beside it), then stop the server. Record the server command, time-to-ready, request latency and the predicted action shape in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "The SGLang server comes up, one multipart POST /v1/actions/generations request for av_0.mp4 returns the predicted action, and outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json holds the 60x9 trajectory; result_summary.md records server command, readiness time, latency and shape.",
      "assertions": [
        "The SGLang server was started with the documented image, model and flags and reported the model before the request was sent",
        "The request was the documented multipart POST /v1/actions/generations with action_mode inverse_dynamics, domain av, raw_action_dim 9 and the bundled av_0.mp4 as input_reference",
        "outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json exists and holds a 60x9 numeric action array taken from the server response (data[0].action.values)",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the action array traces to a real server response in the transcript, and the server was stopped at the end",
        "result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready, request latency and the predicted action shape"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/action_inverse_dynamics_av_custom/av_inverse_0/sample_outputs.json",
          "min_bytes": 2000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "inference request",
        "teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "trtllm-nano-id-av",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano with TensorRT-LLM (trtllm-serve with the single-GPU Nano VisualGen config, guardrails disabled) and run ONE inverse-dynamics request through its synchronous video API for the AV clip bundled by the action entry skill (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/videos/av_0.mp4, relative to this skill directory). Decode the safetensors payload per the skill, saving it as outputs/inverse_dynamics_av.safetensors and the reconstructed clip as outputs/inverse_dynamics_av.mp4, then stop the server. Record the serve command, time-to-ready, request latency and the video / action tensor shapes in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "trtllm-serve hosts Cosmos3-Nano on one GPU, one multipart POST /v1/videos/sync inverse-dynamics request for av_0.mp4 returns a safetensors payload with video, action and frame_rate tensors, saved as outputs/inverse_dynamics_av.safetensors with the decoded clip at outputs/inverse_dynamics_av.mp4; result_summary.md records serve command, readiness time, latency and the tensor shapes.",
      "assertions": [
        "trtllm-serve was launched for nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano with the documented single-GPU VisualGen config and /health answered before the request was sent",
        "The request was the documented multipart POST /v1/videos/sync with format safetensors, response_format file, action_mode inverse_dynamics, domain av and the bundled av_0.mp4 as video_reference; guardrails were disabled via a documented switch rather than acquiring gated access",
        "outputs/inverse_dynamics_av.safetensors exists and decodes to video, action and frame_rate tensors with a 60x9 action, and outputs/inverse_dynamics_av.mp4 was written from the video tensor",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: both files trace to a real server response in the transcript, and the server was stopped at the end",
        "result_summary.md records the serve command, time-to-ready, request latency and the tensor shapes actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/inverse_dynamics_av.safetensors",
          "min_bytes": 1000000
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/inverse_dynamics_av.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 20000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server install + start",
        "readiness",
        "inference request",
        "decode + teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    "HF_TOKEN",
    "GITHUB_TOKEN"
  ],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {
    "minutes": 60,
    "tokens": 3000000
  },
  "setup": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git",
    "dest": "/app/repo",
    "src_mount": "/opt/cosmos-src"
  }
}
